      <!-- Preparation Tips Section -->
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-extrabold text-slate-900 mt-12 mb-4 border-b border-slate-200 pb-2">How to Prepare for Class 10 English Board Examination 2027</h2>
      <p>A good preparation strategy should cover all parts of the English paper. Students should not depend entirely on pairing schemes or guessed questions.</p>
      
      <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4 my-6 not-prose">
        <div class="bg-white border border-slate-200 rounded-xl p-5">
          <h4 class="font-bold text-slate-900 mb-2">1. Prepare the Complete Textbook</h4>
          <p class="text-sm text-slate-600">Read all ten units and both review sections included in your prescribed textbook. Focus on main ideas, exercise questions, vocabulary, and poems.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-white border border-slate-200 rounded-xl p-5">
          <h4 class="font-bold text-slate-900 mb-2">2. Improve English Grammar</h4>
          <p class="text-sm text-slate-600">Practise tenses, forms of verbs, articles, prepositions, active/passive voice, direct/indirect speech, and sentence structure daily.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-white border border-slate-200 rounded-xl p-5">
          <h4 class="font-bold text-slate-900 mb-2">3. Practise Translation Daily</h4>
          <p class="text-sm text-slate-600">Practise both English into Urdu and Urdu into English. Begin with short paragraphs and gradually move to longer passages.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-white border border-slate-200 rounded-xl p-5">
          <h4 class="font-bold text-slate-900 mb-2">4. Prepare Essays and Paragraphs</h4>
          <p class="text-sm text-slate-600">Prepare a collection of useful topics. Understand their main ideas instead of memorizing sentences. Practise within word limits.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-extrabold text-slate-900 mt-10 mb-4 border-b border-slate-200 pb-2">30-Day Class 10 English Preparation Plan</h2>
      <div class="overflow-x-auto w-full max-w-full my-6 border border-slate-200 rounded-lg not-prose">
        <table class="w-full text-left border-collapse text-sm">
          <thead><tr class="bg-slate-100 border-b border-slate-200"><th class="p-3 font-bold text-slate-900">Week</th><th class="p-3 font-bold text-slate-900">Preparation Focus</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody class="divide-y divide-slate-200 text-slate-700">
            <tr class="hover:bg-slate-50"><td class="p-3 font-medium text-slate-900">Week 1</td><td class="p-3">Textbook units, short questions and vocabulary</td></tr>
            <tr class="hover:bg-slate-50"><td class="p-3 font-medium text-slate-900">Week 2</td><td class="p-3">Grammar, narration and pairs of words</td></tr>
            <tr class="hover:bg-slate-50"><td class="p-3 font-medium text-slate-900">Week 3</td><td class="p-3">Translation, essays, paragraphs and poetry</td></tr>
            <tr class="hover:bg-slate-50"><td class="p-3 font-medium text-slate-900">Week 4</td><td class="p-3">Model papers, revision and correcting mistakes</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-extrabold text-slate-900 mt-10 mb-4 border-b border-slate-200 pb-2">Common Mistakes to Avoid in Class 10 English Paper</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 text-sm text-slate-700">
        <li><strong>Studying only selected chapters:</strong> MCQs and other questions can cover a broad range of the prescribed syllabus.</li>
        <li><strong>Ignoring grammar:</strong> Grammar needs regular practice, not last-minute memorization.</li>
        <li><strong>Memorizing translations without understanding:</strong> Learn sentence structure and vocabulary.</li>
        <li><strong>Writing excessively long essays:</strong> Follow the specified word limit.</li>
        <li><strong>Making avoidable spelling mistakes:</strong> Review your written answers.</li>
        <li><strong>Poor time management:</strong> Practise complete papers with a timer.</li>
      </ul>

